            <ArticleTitle>Spinal cord ischaemic stroke associated with vertebral body infarction.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>502-6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Only eight cases of spinal cord ischaemic stroke causing paraplegia with associated vertebral body infarction have been previously described. We describe a ninth case with histopathology confirming the Magnetic Resonance Imaging (MRI) appearance of vertebral body infarction. We have reviewed the literature concerning this condition and discuss its diagnosis and aetiology.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
